{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.05},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"servicing agent and/or the owner and holder\" leaves it indeterminate in what capacity Aurora contracts and whether it holds the Note at all. The \"and/or\" formulation permits either reading of the party's identity and authority.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"a mortgage, deed of trust or comparable security instrument\" identifies the Security Instrument only by an open alternative including the vague word \"comparable\". Which document is the \"Security Instrument\" is therefore established by inference rather than identification.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The definition as written is a fragment — the subject (\"The Note and\") is missing — so grammatically only the Security Instrument is collectively defined as the \"Loan Documents\". Since \"Loan Documents\" drives sections 3, 6, 13 and 21, the omission changes the scope of those provisions.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
     {"issue": "The recital fixes the Arrearage at $13,755.30 as the sum to be repaid, while Attachment A § b states the plan payments will not cure it; whether the Agreement disposes of the stated Arrearage is left open. The itemised figures do reconcile arithmetically, so the tension is with Attachment A rather than internal.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Corporate Advances\" is defined by an open catch-all (\"include, but are not limited to\") over a list of specific servicing fees, so what other charges may be loaded into the Arrearage is unbounded. Whether ejusdem generis confines the category to the enumerated foreclosure/preservation-type fees is exactly what a borrower would contest.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Other Fees\" is defined non-exhaustively (\"include, but are not limited to\") with only two examples, giving the general category no ascertainable boundary. The two specifics are too thin to limit the catch-all by ejusdem generis.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
     {"issue": "This recital asserts as fact that Lender \"has so accelerated and declared due in full\" and \"may have already commenced foreclosure proceedings\", while the immediately following recital states no foreclosure has been commenced and paragraph 8 treats acceleration only conditionally (\"if the Lender previously notified the Customer\"). The recitals and operative paragraph 8 thus point in different directions on whether the loan is in fact accelerated.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": "This recital states no foreclosure proceeding has been commenced and no sale scheduled, yet paragraph 4 addresses postponement of \"a foreclosure sale\" and Lender's freedom not to dismiss \"a pending foreclosure proceeding\", and paragraph 8 speaks of foreclosure resuming \"from the point at which it was placed on hold\". The recital and those operative paragraphs cannot both describe the same state of affairs.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.44}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11},
     {"issue": "The recital assumes \"any foreclosure action that may now be pending\", directly at odds with the preceding recital that Lender \"has not commenced Foreclosure proceedings\" and that no sale has been scheduled. The two consecutive recitals give inconsistent accounts of the foreclosure posture the forbearance operates on.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.15},
     {"issue": "The recital says Lender agreed \"to allow Customer to repay the Arrearage\" under the workout, but Attachment A § b states the aggregate plan payments will be insufficient to pay the Arrearage and the account will remain delinquent. A borrower reading the recital as a promise of a cure meets an operative term that promises the opposite.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.47}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"will not have personal liability on the debt pursuant to this Agreement\" can mean either that no personal liability arises on the underlying debt or only that this Agreement creates none. The qualifier \"pursuant to this Agreement\" attaches ambiguously to \"liability\" or to \"debt\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"forbear from exercising any or all of its rights and remedies\" is ambiguous as to whether Lender must forbear from all remedies or may choose which ones to forbear from. The disjunctive \"any or all\" makes the extent of the only promise Lender gives indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "The forbearance promise sits against paragraph 4 (no obligation to dismiss a pending foreclosure) and paragraph 7 (nothing herein waives the right to commence or resume foreclosure), which together may leave the forbearance with nothing to operate on. Whether Lender actually gave up anything during the term turns on reconciling section 3 with those clauses.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.18},
     {"issue": "The paragraph presupposes a foreclosure sale and \"a pending foreclosure proceeding\", which contradicts the recital stating Lender has not commenced foreclosure proceedings and no sale has been scheduled. It also qualifies section 3's forbearance by relieving Lender of any duty to dismiss.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"or otherwise fails to comply with any of the terms and conditions herein or therein\" is a catch-all sitting on a specific payment-default trigger, so any trivial non-compliance may count as a \"Default\" permitting immediate foreclosure. The parenthetical also miswrites \"any such even\" for \"event\", leaving the defined term's antecedent imprecise.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
   ]}
]}

